## No Double-Cast (`as unknown as`)

### Rule
`as unknown as T` completely bypasses TypeScript's type system. It is **always wrong** — it means the actual runtime type doesn't match the declared type. Fix the underlying mismatch instead.

### Forbidden

```ts
// BAD — found in eventListeners.ts
const lobbyId = (data.lobbyDetails as unknown as { lobbyId: string }).lobbyId;

// BAD — found in ResultScreen.ts
lobbyDetails: undefined as unknown as any;
```

### Fix

```ts
// GOOD — declare the proper type on the data
interface GameTableInfoPayload {
  lobbyDetails: { lobbyId: string; /* ... */ };
}

// Or if the field is truly optional:
const lobbyId = data.lobbyDetails?.lobbyId;
```

If the server sends data in an unexpected shape, fix the type definition to match reality. If the shape genuinely varies, use a discriminated union.

