## No `@ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error`

### Rule
If TypeScript reports a type error, the type is wrong. Fix the type, don't silence the compiler.

### Forbidden

```ts
// BAD — found in NewMatchMakingScreen.ts
// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/ban-ts-comment
// @ts-ignore
someExpression.property;
```

### Exception
`@ts-expect-error` is allowed ONLY in test files where you intentionally test invalid inputs. It must include a comment explaining what error is expected:

```ts
// In tests only:
// @ts-expect-error — testing behavior when invalid type is passed
handleTurnInfo("not a valid payload");
```

