## No `window as any`

### Rule
Never stash global state on `window` with type-unsafe access. If you must use `window` for global variables (webview bridge, debug utilities), declare proper types.

### Forbidden

```ts
// BAD — found in game.ts
let sessionId = (window as any).sessionId;
(window as any).sessionId = email;

// BAD — found in app.init.ts
(globalThis as any).__PIXI_STAGE__ = app.stage;
```

### Fix — Augment the Global Type

```ts
// types/global.d.ts
declare global {
  interface Window {
    sessionId?: string;
    __PIXI_STAGE__?: import("pixi.js").Container;
    __PIXI_RENDERER__?: import("pixi.js").Renderer;
    DebugUtils?: typeof import("../debug").DebugUtils;
  }
}

export {};
```

Now access is type-safe:

```ts
// GOOD — properly typed
window.__PIXI_STAGE__ = app.stage;
const sessionId = window.sessionId;
```

