## Enum Safety

### Rules
- Use `const enum` or `as const` objects for values that don't need runtime reverse-mapping.
- Always handle the `default` case in switch statements on enums — either throw or log.
- Never compare enums with loose equality (`==`). Use strict equality (`===`).

```ts
// BAD
if (CURRENT_PARTNER == PARTNER_ID.gs) { ... }

// GOOD
if (CURRENT_PARTNER === PARTNER_ID.gs) { ... }
```

### Exhaustive Switch

```ts
function getActionLabel(action: ALLOW_ACTIONS): string {
  switch (action) {
    case ALLOW_ACTIONS.HIT: return "Hit";
    case ALLOW_ACTIONS.STAND: return "Stand";
    case ALLOW_ACTIONS.SPLIT: return "Split";
    default: {
      const _exhaustive: never = action;
      throw new Error(`Unhandled action: ${_exhaustive}`);
    }
  }
}
```

