## eslint-disable Rules

### Forbidden Directives
These eslint-disable comments are **never allowed** in production code:

- `/* eslint-disable @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any */`
- `/* eslint-disable @typescript-eslint/ban-ts-comment */`
- `// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-non-null-assertion`

### Allowed (With Justification Comment)
Single-line disables for non-type-safety rules are acceptable when accompanied by a comment explaining why:

```ts
// Pixi's destroy signature accepts boolean | DestroyOptions, ESLint wrongly flags the union
// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-redundant-type-constituents
destroy(options?: boolean | DestroyOptions) { ... }
```
